NOTE: this is sentinel-1's log from run 1, recovered via an ad hoc `docker compose logs
sentinel-1 --since 5m` check run immediately after the test (before the script's own
--force-recreate at the start of run 2 destroyed this container instance). It's a genuine,
correctly-sourced partial record -- sentinel-1's own view, NOT the elected leader's (sentinel-1
was never the leader in run 1; the leader was runid ec7394d3f2ac8eedb37495e873ebbf5a97128f14,
whose own logs are NOT recoverable -- that container no longer exists, and the script's log-save
step had a timestamp-format bug on this run that produced an empty file instead of capturing it
in time). The leader's own reasoning for why 2 consecutive failover epochs failed to complete is
genuinely lost. Preserved here anyway because the overall event sequence (odown, epoch
progression, sustained DNS-resolution failures throughout each failover window, eventual +reboot
once the primary was manually restarted) is still real, valid evidence from this run.

